"""
Module handling word-for-word translation of Latin Vulgate Bible to English.

translateLatin( htmlStr:str ) -> str
    Do basic word-for-word translation from Latin Vulgate Bible to English.
briefDemo() -> None
fullDemo() -> None
main calls fullDemo()


Maintenance instructions from the project owner (for future AI passes):
    * Expand ordinary vocabulary coverage across the whole Vulgate, including rare
      and inflected forms. TEST books and reported examples are starting points,
      not the scope of a pass. Inspect the original Latin and the actual English
      output: apparent misspellings can be fragments created by an earlier
      replacement, rather than untranslated Latin words.
    * Use the Latin meaning appropriate to the Vulgate passage. Check uncertain
      readings, inflections, and source spellings in their verse context and
      historical references; resemblance to an English word is not sufficient
      evidence for a translation.
    * Concentrate on ordinary words when reviewing spelling-error lists. Ignore
      names, especially expected English name forms beginning with Y, and preserve
      existing name translations. Valid English words and regional spellings do
      not automatically require a new Latin translation entry.
    * Keep the table in general alphabetical order by the Latin source form,
      with longer forms before shorter forms that could consume their prefixes.
      Preserve necessary phrase and replacement-order exceptions, including rules
      that consume intermediate spellings. Respect case-sensitive matching.
    * Do not enumerate trailing punctuation without a reason. An unrestricted
      source form already matches before punctuation: forms such as missa,
      tribuet, Scuto, and scuto do not need separate punctuation entries merely
      because punctuation follows them. Guard a form only when it could damage a
      longer English word used elsewhere as a translation, or when a demonstrated
      replacement dependency requires it. For example, guard tribu if an English
      translation beginning with tribu is actually used; verify that collision
      rather than assuming it. Check longer words and replacement chains before
      removing guards, and delete obsolete commented-out entries.
    * Alternative translations may be separated by forward slashes, with the more
      likely/common meaning first (e.g., 'branch/twig'); use alternatives sparingly.
      Add a part of speech when it helps disambiguate an English gloss, using
      conventions such as love(n), love(v), fair(aj), and fair(n).
    * Check punctuation and HTML boundaries, capitalisation, longer-word
      collisions, and repeated or damaged English glosses. Review whole-corpus
      changes and retain focused regression cases for reported misses and
      historical meanings.

CHANGELOG:
    2026-10-20 Complete residual inflections and translate a damaged scapegoat phrase from its explicit source gloss
    2026-10-19 Document the owner's instructions for future vocabulary passes
    2026-10-17 Add septena and complete plurima/ululate forms; clarify plural fault and charge glosses
    2026-10-17 Distinguish noun, verb, and adjective senses in ambiguous English glosses
    2026-10-17 Fix whole-Bible residual forms, ordinal typos, and commentary abbreviations
    2026-10-17 Fix remaining TEST vocabulary and shorter-word replacement collisions
    2025-03-20 Moved into BOS from OBD (OpenBibleData)
    2026-10-16 Expanded Latin forms from PSA/MAT/MRK spelling checks; ordered longer forms before prefixes
    2026-10-16 Split German and Latin translations into separate modules
    2026-10-16 Expanded Latin translations from whole-Bible spelling results; protected English glosses
"""
